  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5529",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to OAW-28 through a series of molecular interactions involving purinoceptors and a compound that acts as a target. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin targets P2X purinoceptor 1, which is subsequently targeted by [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, a compound that also targets OAW-28. This pathway is corroborated by another route where doxorubicin directly targets NCI-H46, which is similarly targeted by the same compound and also binds to OAW-28. A third pathway links doxorubicin to palmarumycin CP18, which also targets OAW-28. These findings collectively indicate that doxorubicin exerts its effects on OAW-28 via a mechanism involving a purinoceptor-targeted compound, suggesting a potential role in modulating cellular processes through this pathway. The consistency across multiple target links supports the hypothesis that doxorubicin interacts with OAW-28 through a shared molecular mechanism involving purinoceptor engagement.",
